ion layout-engine-section background-width--full-bleed section-height--custom content-width--wide horizontal-alignment--center vertical-alignment--middle white-bold", "style": null, "rect": [3514, 1086], "minHeight": "1080px", "padTop": "0px", "padBot": "0px", "bgc": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)", "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)", "cwPad": ["0px", "0px", "0px", "0px"], "cwStyle": "padding-top: calc(0vmax / 10); padding-bottom: calc(0vmax / 10);", "bg": null, "overlay": null, "inFooter": false, "blocks": [{"id": "fe-block-4da0225a77cec082c2c4", "area": "8 / 2 / 11 / 12", "z": "1", "rect": [58, 3785, 746, 116], "type": "sqs-block website-component-block html-block", "jc": "flex-start", "ai": "normal", "fd": "column", "pad": "0px", "disp": "block", "html": "<h2 style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-fs=\"38.1184px\" data-lh=\"37.3877px\" data-m=\"0px 0px\" data-col=\"rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Hiking the Norwegian Fjell<span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--black\" data-color=\"rgb(0, 0, 0)\" data-td=\"none\" data-fw=\"500\"> <br></span><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--darkAccent\" data-color=\"rgb(147, 149, 152)\" data-td=\"none\" data-fw=\"500\">A Journey in Norw with Vandra™</span></h2>", "htmlRect": [58, 3785, 746, 75]}, {"id": "fe-block-480f51f0a3a9506b33b3", "area": "12 / 2 / 21 / 13", "z": "0", "rect": [58, 3940, 820, 349], "type": "sqs-block website-component-block html-block", "jc": "flex-start", "ai": "normal", "fd": "column", "pad": "0px", "disp": "block", "html": "<h4 style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-fs=\"15.5392px\" data-lh=\"15.8627px\" data-m=\"0px 32px\" data-col=\"rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--darkAccent\" data-color=\"rgb(147, 149, 152)\" data-td=\"none\" data-fw=\"500\">Into the highlands<br></span>In early summer, Djani and Melissa set off with their daughter Bella on a trail through the Norwegian highlands. Starting in the Hemsedal valley, they moved between open plateaus and narrow birch forests, following the quiet pulse of the land. Their goal wasn’t a summit — it was the stillness between the climbs, the unspoken moments when Bella’s laughter echoed into the wide sky. What they found was not just space to walk, but space to be.</h4><h4 style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-fs=\"15.5392px\" data-lh=\"15.8627px\" data-m=\"32px 32px\" data-col=\"rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--darkAccent\" data-color=\"rgb(147, 149, 152)\" data-td=\"none\" data-fw=\"500\">Less weight, more presence<br></span>Crossing shallow rivers and winding through highland moss, they carried only what they needed — and noticed more because of it. “We stopped thinking about what we were carrying,” Djani said. “It just worked.” The Vandra™ system moved with them, not against them: weatherproof, balanced, and adaptable as the terrain shifted. It didn’t just carry Bella. It kept the rhythm of the day.</h4><h4 style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-fs=\"15.5392px\" data-lh=\"15.8627px\" data-m=\"32px 0px\" data-col=\"rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--darkAccent\" data-color=\"rgb(147, 149, 152)\" data-td=\"none\" data-fw=\"500\">When the light lingers<br></span>One moment brought sun over snow patches, the next a soft drizzle through clouded skies. But their pace never faltered. With modular compartments and a snug, weatherproof frame, Vandra™ kept Bella close, dry, and content. “We didn’t need to hurry,” Melissa said. “Everything we needed was already with us.” The journey wasn’t about reaching somewhere — it was about what stayed with them along the way.</h4>", "htmlRect": [58, 3940, 820, 302]}, {"id": "fe-block-85c38697161e55e8f6c3", "area": "6 / 18 / 24 / 25", "z": "3", "rect": [1251, 3707, 522, 698], "type": "sqs-block website-component-block image-block", "jc": "center", "ai": "normal", "fd": "column", "pad": "0px", "disp": "block", "img": {"src": "20250324_142713046_iOS.png", "fit": "cover", "radius": "0px", "pos": "50% 50%", "w": 522, "h": 698, "wrapRadius": "20px", "wrapOverflow": "hidden", "wrap": [1251, 3707, 522, 698]}}],